  "full_response": "# **Ultimate Guide to Building a Full-Stack Web Application from Scratch**\n\nThis tutorial will guide you through building a **full-stack web application** from the ground up, covering:\n\n1. **Frontend Development** (React, TypeScript, State Management)\n2. **Backend Development** (Node.js, Express, REST/GraphQL APIs)\n3. **Database Design & Integration** (PostgreSQL, MongoDB, ORMs)\n4. **Authentication & Authorization** (JWT, OAuth, Sessions)\n5. **Deployment** (Docker, AWS, CI/CD)\n6. **Testing** (Unit, Integration, E2E)\n7. **Monitoring & Logging** (Prometheus, Grafana, ELK Stack)\n8. **Security Best Practices** (OWASP, HTTPS, Rate Limiting)\n\n---\n\n## **1. Project Setup & Planning**\n### **1.1 Define Requirements**\n- **Purpose**: What problem does your app solve?\n- **Features**: List core functionalities (e.g., user auth, CRUD operations).\n- **Tech Stack**: Choose based on scalability, team expertise, and project needs.\n\n### **1.2 Tech Stack Selection**\n| **Category**       | **Technology**                          |\n|--------------------|----------------------------------------|\n| **Frontend**       | React, TypeScript, Vite, TailwindCSS   |\n| **Backend**        | Node.js, Express, TypeScript           |\n| **Database**       | PostgreSQL (Relational), MongoDB (NoSQL) |\n| **Authentication** | JWT, OAuth (Google/GitHub), Sessions   |\n| **Deployment**     | Docker, AWS (EC2, RDS, S3), CI/CD      |\n| **Testing**        | Jest, React Testing Library, Cypress   |\n| **Monitoring**     | Prometheus, Grafana, Winston           |\n| **Security**       | Helmet, CORS, Rate Limiting, OWASP     |\n\n---\n\n## **2. Frontend Development**\n### **2.1 Initialize React App with Vite**\n```bash\nnpm create vite@latest frontend -- --template react-ts\ncd frontend\nnpm install\nnpm install axios react-router-dom @tanstack/react-query tailwindcss postcss autoprefixer\nnpm run dev\n```\n\n### **2.2 Folder Structure**\n```\nfrontend/\n├── src/\n│   ├── components/    # Reusable UI components\n│   ├── pages/         #",
